Reason:
The bug occurs because the code assumes that XRC (Extended Reliable Connection) support is available and attempts to create and register an XRC receive queue pair (QP) using the `qp_num` from `lcl_ep->xrc_recv_qp`. In systems lacking XRC support, this leads to build errors as the necessary attributes and functions for XRC are not available.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
ret = ibv_reg_xrc_rcv_qp(openib_btl->device->xrc_domain, lcl_ep->xrc_recv_qp_num);
ret = ibv_create_xrc_rcv_qp(&qp_init_attr, &lcl_ep->xrc_recv_qp_num);
```
Reason:
The fix introduces proper handling for systems without XRC support by using `lcl_ep->xrc_recv_qp_num` instead of `lcl_ep->xrc_recv_qp->qp_num`. This ensures that the code correctly registers and creates the receive queue pair without relying on XRC-specific attributes, thus preventing build errors in environments lacking XRC support.

